{
  "_comment": [
    "Curated logo sources, keyed by the team name Liquipedia uses.",
    "",
    "This file contains URLs, not artwork. It ships with the project; the images",
    "it points at do not, and are fetched to each user's own machine and cached",
    "there. Preferring an org's own CDN over Liquipedia also spreads the load",
    "across many hosts rather than concentrating it on one, which is what got",
    "this project rate-limited in the first place.",
    "",
    "'terms' records what the source actually states. 'none stated' is the honest",
    "and dominant answer: almost no esports org publishes a press kit with reuse",
    "terms, so most entries are simply the file the org's own site loads. Where a",
    "real licence exists it is recorded, along with any attribution it requires.",
    "",
    "Verified: every url returned HTTP 200 with an image content-type when added.",
    "source values: official (org's own site), presskit, commons (usually PD-textlogo), wikipedia-nonfree (fair use scoped to Wikipedia — legally no broader than Liquipedia's own copy), other."
  ],
